# ── credentials ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing under api_key/ is ever committed. The loaders in code/llm_client.py read these files at
# runtime and fall back to environment variables; there is no key in tracked source.
api_key/
*.key
.env
CLAUDE.local.md

# ── licensed source data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# UMLS requires a UTS licence and its agreement restricts redistribution. cui_to_tui.csv is a
# 443,700-row dump of UMLS CUI→semantic-type mappings, so publishing it would redistribute
# licensed content. Regenerate it from your own licensed Neo4j instance — see README.
cui_to_tui.csv
cui_with_terms.csv
*_umls_*.csv

# ── large artefacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ~1.9 GB total, and all of it is regenerable: cache/ from Neo4j + the LLM, frozen/ from
# run_stage_a.sh, results/ from run_reader.py. A clone should be code, not outputs.
cache/
frozen/
results/
logs/
prompt_dumps/
oneshot/
*.pkl
*.pt
*.zip
*.jsonl.bak*

# datasets/ holds derived benchmark files plus the hand-review labels. The labels are the part
# worth versioning — 723 per-question verdicts that no script regenerates — so they come back in.
# NB: the pattern excludes the CONTENTS (datasets/*/*), not the directory (datasets/*/). git will
# not descend into an excluded directory, so a `!` re-include underneath one never takes effect.
datasets/*/*
!datasets/*/temporal_critical.json

# _raw_* are download caches, not sources: build_new_dataset.py fetches each one over the network
# when it is missing (MedBullets CSV, MedMCQA and MMLU via the HF datasets-server). Shipping 4 MB
# of someone else's corpus adds nothing a clone cannot fetch itself.
datasets/_raw_*

# ── python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/

# ── os ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
